I didn't include the two operations requests. This node's declared capabilities are only `aap:caps/inference-llm`. On `wasm32-unknown-unknown` without a WASI adapter, the component has no file access to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. Fetching `metadata.internal.example` would need an `http-client` import, which would give the node outbound authority it wasn't granted and send item text to a host outside its scope. If operations wants either behavior, it should be granted explicitly in the graph, for example as an `http-client` handle scoped to that host or a logging capability, and then the node's import list can change. The code below implements only the summarisation.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{classified-item, item-verdict};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(classified: classified-item) -> item-verdict;
}
```

